  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Outdoor music for weddings, saints' feasts and village dances across North Macedonia, Kosovo and southern Serbia, played mostly by professional Roma musicians. Zurlas, loud conical double-reed shawms, are played in pairs, one leading the ornamented melody with circular breathing while the other holds a drone, over the tapan, a large double-headed drum beaten with a heavy stick on one head and a thin switch on the other; it is the classic accompaniment of dances such as teškoto.",
